# ac3 - the matrix must be INTERNALLY consistent and REPRODUCIBLE. Every count
# the fence checks is DERIVED from the document's own REQ_ROW lines and compared
# to the summary lines the generator prints, so a hand-edited summary, a dropped
# row or a re-labelled status all RED. The generator is then run TWICE and must
# land on byte-identical bytes (it is deterministic by contract: no timestamps,
# no git metadata), and it must exit 0 - the fail-closed fence means rc!=0 is a
# real GAP/unpointed-row product failure, never something the refresh may hide.
